---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="Fieldwork"
	description="Gavin Keulks — site-based photographs and conference papers toward a book on the reclamation of traumatic spaces in Ireland."
>
	<div class="wrap">
		<header class="page-head">
			<h1>Fieldwork</h1>
			<p class="page-intro">
				Toward a book on the reclamation of traumatic spaces in Ireland.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="project">
			<p>
				Site-based photographs, my own, of places rather than people: Magdalene
				laundries and mother and baby homes, the ghost estates left by the collapse
				of the Celtic&nbsp;Tiger, and the contested walls of Belfast.
			</p>
			<p>
				They are working toward my final scholarly book, on how such spaces in
				Ireland and Northern&nbsp;Ireland are reclaimed, memorialized, or left to
				stand. The argument has been taking shape in conference papers since 2014.
				The book itself is not yet written, and the photographs are still being
				prepared for publication here.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="strand">
			<h2>Magdalene Laundries and Mother and Baby Homes</h2>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Home (Dis)Rule: Magdalene Laundries, Mother and Baby Homes, and
						Ghost Estates.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					American Conference for Irish Studies. Denver,&nbsp;CO, 2026.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Ireland&rsquo;s Last Magdalene Laundry.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Northeast Modern Language Association. Boston,&nbsp;MA, 2024.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Excavating History: Justice for Irish Magdalenes.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Northeast Modern Language Association. Niagara,&nbsp;NY, 2023.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="strand">
			<h2>Ghost Estates and Topographical Scars</h2>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Irish Spatial Texts and Topographical Scars.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Northeast Modern Language Association. Philadelphia,&nbsp;PA, 2025.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Thwarted Alchemy: Irish Ghost Estates and Post-Celtic-Tiger
						Literature.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Humanities and Education Research Association. Chicago,&nbsp;IL, 2018.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Topographical Scars: Economic Collapse, Mass Emigration, and
						Irish Tourism.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Popular and American Culture Association. New&nbsp;Orleans,&nbsp;LA, 2015.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Trauma Memorials and Historical Geography: Ghost Estates as
						Modern-day Famine Walls.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Transatlantic Connections&nbsp;II. Donegal, Ireland, 2015.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section class="strand">
			<h2>Belfast, Dublin, and Contested Space</h2>
			<ul class="cite-list">
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Politics and the Humanities in Belfast Street Art.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Humanities and Education Research Association. Chicago,&nbsp;IL, 2020.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;An Art-walk in Belfast: Stepping beyond Politics.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					American Conference for Irish Studies. Boston,&nbsp;MA, 2019.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Slouching towards Belfast to be Born: Apolitical Street-art in
						Belfast.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Popular and American Culture Association. Washington,&nbsp;DC, 2019.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;Between the Lanes: Politics and the Humanities in Irish
						Street-art.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					Humanities and Education Research Association. San&nbsp;Diego,&nbsp;CA,
					2017.
				</li>
				<li>
					<span class="cite-title"
						>&ldquo;&lsquo;What Rough Beast&rsquo;: Integrated and Conflicted Spaces
						in Dublin.&rdquo;</span
					>{' '}
					American Conference on Irish Studies. Dublin, Ireland, 2014.
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page-head {
		padding-block: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 6.5rem) clamp(1.75rem, 4vw, 3rem);
	}

	.page-head h1 {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}

	.page-intro {
		font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 1rem + 0.6vw, 1.3rem);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
		text-wrap: balance;
	}

	.project {
		padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 3.75rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.project p {
		margin: 0 0 1.15rem;
	}

	.project p:last-child {
		margin-bottom: 0;
	}

	.strand {
		padding-block: clamp(2.25rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.strand:last-child {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.strand h2 {
		margin: 0 0 1.35rem;
	}

	.cite-list {
		list-style: none;
		margin: 0;
		padding: 0;
		max-width: 42rem;
	}

	.cite-list li {
		padding-block: 0.7rem;
		padding-left: 1.4rem;
		text-indent: -1.4rem;
		font-size: 1rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--color-ink-soft);
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}

	.cite-list li + li {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
	}

	.cite-title {
		color: var(--color-ink);
	}
</style>
